This work uses simulated benchmarks with public datasets and checkpoints and involves no human
subjects or sensitive data.

\subsection*{Reproducibility statement}
We will release anonymised code as supplementary material. It covers dataset encoding, TDR
training, graph construction, critic training, and CEM evaluation, together with the driver
scripts used to produce every table. We will also release the fixed task-pool files and the
trained TDR, graph, and critic for every seed. All experiments use the public LeWM checkpoints
and datasets \citep{lewm}. Episodes that contain evaluation tasks are excluded from all
learned-asset training and calibration. \Cref{sec:setup} describes the protocols and seeds,
\cref{app:algorithm} the planning procedure, \cref{app:hyperparams} all hyperparameters
(including the unchanged CEM configuration), and \cref{tab:compute} compute costs. Live
frames must be rendered with the MuJoCo version that produced the dataset
(\cref{app:render}); we pin MuJoCo 3.5.0 and dm\_control 1.0.37 for Reacher.

